@startuml
' One complete sequence diagram, intentionally retaining participant-level messages.
skinparam backgroundColor #0B1020
skinparam DefaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam DefaultFontColor #F1F6FF
skinparam DefaultFontSize 14
skinparam TitleFontColor #F5F9FF
skinparam TitleFontSize 20
skinparam Shadowing false
skinparam RoundCorner 9
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #1F3654
  ParticipantBorderColor #8DBAFF
  ParticipantFontColor #F1F6FF
  ParticipantFontSize 13
  ActorBackgroundColor #15556A
  ActorBorderColor #64D9F2
  ActorFontColor #F1F6FF
  ArrowColor #A4C4F3
  ArrowFontColor #F1F6FF
  ArrowFontSize 12
  LifeLineBorderColor #6583A8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #19283E
  GroupBorderColor #8769BE
  GroupFontColor #F1F6FF
  GroupHeaderFontColor #FFFFFF
  GroupHeaderBackgroundColor #392854
  GroupBackgroundColor #101D30
  NoteBackgroundColor #25334B
  NoteBorderColor #83A1C8
  NoteFontColor #F1F6FF
  NoteFontSize 12
  DividerBackgroundColor #213B5B
  DividerBorderColor #718FBA
  DividerFontColor #F1F6FF
  DividerFontSize 14
}

title DocMind — Document processing and LLM analysis

actor "Client" as Client #15556A
participant "FastAPI" as API #15556A
database "PostgreSQL" as PG #163F35
queue "RabbitMQ" as MQ #392854
participant "Celery" as Worker #193A67
participant "ClamAV" as AV #622C39
database "S3 / MinIO" as S3 #57401F
database "MongoDB" as Mongo #163F35
database "Redis" as Redis #512C32
participant "FastStream" as Stream #392854
participant "LLM" as LLM #563049

== 1. Upload and SHA-256 deduplication ==
Client -> API: POST /documents/\nfile, provider
activate API
API -> API: Validate, save shared temp file\nCalculate SHA-256
API -> PG: Find reusable file by hash
PG --> API: File candidates
opt Reusable file candidates found
  API -> Mongo: Look for reusable raw text
  Mongo --> API: Raw text (if available)
end
API -> PG: Create NEW user-owned Document

alt FULL_PIPELINE: no reusable binary
  API -> MQ: Queue antivirus task\n(or upload task if AV disabled)
else EXTRACTION_ONLY: binary exists
  API -> PG: Reuse file_key\nDocument status = uploaded
  API -> MQ: Queue extraction task
else ANALYSIS_ONLY: binary + text exist
  API -> Mongo: Copy raw text to new Document
  alt Copy successful
    API -> PG: Document status = extracted
    API -> Mongo: Create DocumentAnalysis (queued)
    API -> MQ: Publish AnalysisRequestedEvent
  else Raw-text copy failed
    API -> PG: Document status = uploaded
    API -> MQ: Queue extraction task
  end
end
API --> Client: 201 Created (DocumentResponse)
deactivate API

note over API,Mongo
Every upload creates a new Document.\nMatching hashes never reuse completed LLM results.
end note

== 2. Antivirus (FULL_PIPELINE when enabled) ==
opt Antivirus is enabled
  MQ -> Worker: Consume antivirus task
  activate Worker
  Worker -> PG: Document status = scanning
  Worker -> AV: Scan local file (INSTREAM)
  AV --> Worker: Scan result
  alt Clean or configured fail-open
    Worker -> MQ: Queue S3 upload task
  else Infected
    Worker -> PG: Document status = infected
    Worker -> Worker: Cleanup temp file
  else Unavailable, fail-closed
    Worker -> PG: Document status = failed
    Worker -> Worker: Cleanup temp file
  end
  deactivate Worker
end

== 3. Object storage (FULL_PIPELINE if processing continues) ==
opt Upload task was queued
  MQ -> Worker: Consume upload task
  activate Worker
  Worker -> PG: Document status = uploading
  Worker -> S3: Upload binary
  S3 --> Worker: Upload successful
  Worker -> PG: Save file_key\nDocument status = uploaded
  Worker -> MQ: Queue extraction task
  deactivate Worker
end

== 4. Text extraction ==
opt Extraction task was queued
  MQ -> Worker: Consume extraction task
  activate Worker
  Worker -> PG: Document status = extracting
  Worker -> Worker: Extract from shared local temp file
  opt File missing (file_not_found)
    Worker -> S3: Restore binary by file_key
    S3 --> Worker: File downloaded
    Worker -> Worker: Retry extraction from restored file
  end
  Worker -> Mongo: Upsert raw text for Document
  Worker -> PG: Document status = extracted\nClear temp_filename
  Worker -> Worker: Cleanup temp file
  Worker -> Mongo: Create/get DocumentAnalysis (queued)
  Worker -> MQ: Publish AnalysisRequestedEvent\n(analysis_id, document_id, user_id, request_id)
  deactivate Worker
end

note over PG,Mongo
File processing completes at Document.extracted.\nAn analysis failure does not change Document status.
end note

== 5. Independent LLM analysis ==
opt AnalysisRequestedEvent was published
  MQ -> Stream: Deliver analysis event
  activate Stream
  Stream -> Mongo: Load existing DocumentAnalysis + raw text
  Stream -> Redis: Get cached active prompt
  alt Cache miss
    Stream -> Mongo: Load active prompt
    Stream -> Redis: Cache prompt
  end
  Stream -> Mongo: Analysis status = analyzing
  Stream -> LLM: Analyze text with selected provider
  alt Successful response
    LLM --> Stream: LLM result
    Stream -> Mongo: Save result + prompt version\nAnalysis status = success
  else Permanent failure
    Stream -> Mongo: Analysis status = failed\nfailure_kind = permanent
  else Retryable failure
    Stream -> Stream: Retry same Analysis\n(up to configured limit)
    opt Retries exhausted
      Stream -> Mongo: Analysis status = failed\nfailure_kind = transient
    end
  end
  deactivate Stream
end
note over Mongo
Manual retry of failed/transient analysis creates a NEW\nDocumentAnalysis linked via retry_of_analysis_id.
end note

== 6. Read results / download ==
Client -> API: GET /documents/{id}
activate API
API -> PG: Load Document metadata
API -> Mongo: Load text + analyses
API --> Client: DocumentResponse with analyses
deactivate API

Client -> API: GET /documents/{id}/download
activate API
API -> PG: Get authorized Document + file_key
API -> S3: Generate presigned download URL
S3 --> API: Presigned URL
API --> Client: download_url
deactivate API

@enduml
